  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 5.1.0. ISchedulingOutboxStore is the opt-in an outbox store declares to hold notifications scheduled for later delivery (CreatedAt and NextRetryAt at the due time); a store without it keeps working for everything else. OutboxBacklog.ScheduledCount counts the scheduled messages not yet due, which PendingCount and the lag leave out.\n            A context built with the parameterless RequestContextBase() constructor inside a context factory the dispatcher calls reads the application's TimeProvider, so the dispatch reads the clock once.\n            CQRSharp.Transports, experimental (CQREXP001): INotificationTransport and INotificationIntake, the extension point a message-broker transport such as CQRSharp.RabbitMQ builds on. The analyzers treat CQRSharp.RabbitMQ as CQRSharp's own package.\n            Fixed: the CQRA018/CQRA019 (statement lambda) and CQRA020 code fixes write the file's own line endings, not the platform's: on Windows they wrote CRLF into a file with LF line endings.\n            See https://github.com/BisocM/CQRSharp/blob/v5.1.0/CHANGELOG.md for the full notes; upgrading from 5.0 needs no code or schema change.",
